<title>ITALY: Italy's Dini says would have preferred EMU delay.</title>
<headline>Italy's Dini says would have preferred EMU delay.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian Foreign Minister Lamberto Dini said on Tuesday he would have preferred to see the launch of European monetary and economic union put back by a year, but added that he now saw no chance of negotiating a delay.</p>
<p>Dini told Reuters Financial Television there was &quot;a better than even chance&quot; that the single European currency would begin as scheduled in 1999.</p>
</text>
